      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "An additional feature that could be useful is the ability to have a distance+3d direction vector for each player.  Players would have the option in security settings to disable showing their distance+vector for different trust levels.\nThis would help you find friends and other players in larger, more populated instances; while having the option to hide your distance+vector based on trust level (or at the very least an everyone, friends-only, no one trinary option) would help people avoid players seeking to harass others based on avatar/gender/etc.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-04T07:57:00.048Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "”Scoreboard”-like Menu-wing with a compact player list for users in the current instance containing stats for each individual user.\nStats like:\n- Names in trust-rank colors\n- Avatar optimization rank\n- PC/Quest\n- Ping\n- FPS\nCould make things like FPS or Ping etc togglable if you dont care about that stuff.\nThis feature used to exist in a mod called ”PlayerList” and was also in the EMMVRC mod before the UI update. \nTo check this kind of information with the mod used to take 2 seconds.\nNow it takes 5 minutes/you cant see the info at all depending on what you wanna see.\n=====\nIt was very useful when joining an instance to quickly check if this was a place worth staying in or not based on the people in there.\nIt was also super useful for events and event staff when enforcing optimized avatars.\nIt was also very useful to see if there are malicious users/bots/crashers joining the instance, often allowed you to get out before they could crash your game/computer.",
